		"meta": {
			"author": "",
			"category": "source",
			"deploymentTarget": {
				"branch": "",
				"name": "Wire",
				"version": {
					"major": 7,
					"minor": 23,
					"patch": 0
				}
			},
			"description": "Rolling Landscape v2 - Art Deco night skyline of the 1930s as parallax silhouettes. Nothing moves by itself: drive 'Scroll' from Arena (BPM Sync or Timeline). Scroll Dir: Left\/Right. Parallax: how much slower the back layers move (0 = all equal). Layer Count 0-6: layers are added from back to front; fractional values fade the next layer in, so it can follow FFT smoothly. Layer 1-6 On switch single layers off regardless of Layer Count. Layers 1-2: towers (stepped, crown with needle, mast, fan crown, slab). Layers 3-4: city (water tower, radio mast, theatre, department store, bridge pylon). Layers 5-6: street level (elevated railway with train, street lamps, power station, neon sign). Density: share of filled plots. Horizon: base height. Seed: a different value gives a different city. Each layer has its own color (Layer 1 = back). Window Lights: share of lit windows, one Window Color for all. Moon: On, X \/ Y (screen units, Y -1 = bottom, X about -1.78..1.78; the moon sits behind the skyline, so animating Moon Y from about -0.9 upwards gives a moonrise), Opacity, Size, Color. Searchlights: number of beams 0-6 (fractional fades the next one in, beams sweep with Scroll), Beam Color. Airships: number 0-3 (fractional fades in, they drift with Scroll), Airship Dir Left \/ Right \/ Random (Random picks a direction per airship, changes with Seed), Airship Color. Backdrop On\/Off: colored sky or transparent. Drawn by the ISF shader RollingLandscape.fs in the patch folder (must stay next to the patch).",
			"displayName": "Rolling Landscape v2",
			"identifier": "3473280c-9853-4744-8083-c8dbbaba536b",
			"licenseName": "",
			"mail": "",
